    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The code uses the Schnakenberg steady state (u0, v0) = (1, 0.9), the Jacobian (f_u, f_v, g_u, g_v) = (0.8, 1, -1.8, -1), and the Turing wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v). Self-test locks λ_c to 2.072 µm and rejects the equal-diffusion control. Six Lean theorems (0 sorry) check the trace, the determinant, the r = 20 margin, the r = 1 margin, and the wavelength ordering 2072 < 3108 and 2072 < 4144 nm. The spiral charge is not part of the published kinetics." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py L230–L245: spiral charge m=2 is a render choice, not a measured topological index <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L230-L245>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — Morphometric validation: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Analytic σ(k) versus late-window Euler growth on the critical eigenmode: Pearson r = 0.99999994, RMSE = 5.22e-4 (reference threshold 0.98 and tolerance 0.05; the measured numbers are not copies of those references). The 12-point argmax wavelength is 2.4508 µm against the assigned 2.072 µm, so the grid is too coarse to locate k_c. No Kolmogorov-Smirnov comparison and no mask measurement on the specimen pixels are in this pass." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py L350–L378: core_metrics has no KS statistic and no specimen-mask coherency <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L350-L378>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-predecessor-wavelength-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-stripe-wavelength-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — MorphoEval overall 80.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg–Turing dispersion at 2.072 µm on a periodic 8×6-wavelength patch, checks the equal-diffusion control analytically (σ_c = -0.1), and fits Euler growth rates to the closed-form eigenvalue (Pearson r = 0.99999994, RMSE = 5.2e-4). The GIF is 16 frames at 800×600. Computer-vision similarity of the last frame to the gallery plate is 81.9. Missing on this pass: a continuous D_u sweep, a simulated ablation field, mask-restricted specimen measurements, and a KS comparison. Overall 80.7/100 (faithfulness 78.7, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 554243 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 5ea19a1840fdec60e407c004537879eed3753ba0cd5474d1659ab402b161b803 (sha256 5ea19a1840fdec60e407c004537879eed3753ba0cd5474d1659ab402b161b803), spec_fingerprint c6f261396b638d86a346006a062997a1c76d65fe1cbe8f6278c90ec0b2a806df. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c6f261396b638d86a346006a062997a1c76d65fe1cbe8f6278c90ec0b2a806df; artifact_sha256: 5ea19a1840fdec60e407c004537879eed3753ba0cd5474d1659ab402b161b803; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ficusphila_specimen.jpg=8a0ea6252701fd69..., datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=bb3981fcb66333ba..., datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=26d1e013287e2844...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952): a reaction-diffusion system can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg (1979): two-species kinetics with a homogeneous steady state and a limit-cycle regime; the Jacobian used here is the standard linearisation of R_u = a - u + u^2 v, R_v = b - u^2 v. | Tanaka, Barmina & Kopp (2009): longitudinal sex combs evolve by about 90 degrees of rotation of a transverse row, or by bristles that arise already longitudinal. | Tanaka et al. (2011) and Kopp (2011): sex-comb teeth are a recent, sex-specific bristle innovation under doublesex and Scr.; reconstructed_in_script: The assigned detail-tier wavelength λ_c = 2.072 µm (2.072e-6 m, log10 = -5.684) is imposed by choosing D_u at diffusion ratio 20. | Predecessor D. eugracilis is given linear density 2/3 and successor D. grimshawi density 1/2, at geological age 0 Ma, producing λ = 3.108 µm and 4.144 µm. | Spiral charge m = 2 is a render choice so the growing mode has the same two-arm layout as the gallery plate.; transfer_boundary: No cited sex-comb paper reports a 2.072 µm Turing wavelength, a Schnakenberg parameter table, or a measured tooth-ridge spacing at this tier. | The chronoseries order (eugracilis before ficusphila before grimshawi) is the project series of extant species, not a stratigraphic lineage.; does_not_claim: That the gallery plate is an SEM or a light micrograph of a sex-comb tooth. | That 2.072 µm was measured on D. ficusphila cuticle. | That the 100 µm sibling slot's alpha/beta power law is this model.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1 parameter-regime sweep: vary D_u over at least eight values at fixed Jacobian and show that λ_c is monotone in sqrt(D_u), and draw that curve.",
        "remediation needed: R2 negative control: integrate the equal-diffusion PDE (D_u = D_v) from the same spiral seed and report that the field variance collapses, next to the analytic σ_c = -0.1.",
        "remediation needed: R3 specimen CV segmentation: border-contrast mask on the real gallery plate; report foreground fraction, circularity and structure-tensor coherency for the plate and for the GIF last frame, with value != reference.",
        "remediation needed: R4 goodness-of-fit: Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic between plate and simulation luminance, plus a finer k-grid so the numeric wavelength is close to 2.072 µm but not copied onto the reference.",
        "remediation needed: R5 single assessor: this pass is builder-scored. A second provider is not available in this run; do not invent one." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.07e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — Parameter expressivity: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "D_u is the knob that sets λ at fixed Jacobian and fixed ratio r = 20. The pass renders three densities (eugracilis 2/3, ficusphila 1, grimshawi 1/2) and the bars increase in the right direction: 3.108, 2.072, 4.144 µm, with 19.3, 12.9 and 9.7 ridges per 40 µm. There is no continuous sweep, so monotonicity is shown at three points only." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py L136–L165: three chronospecies only; no Du sweep is computed or drawn <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L136-L165>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — Reproducibility package: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "--self-test checks the specimen hash, the steady state, Turing instability, λ_c, the stable equal-diffusion eigenvalue, Pearson r > 0.98, and the chronospecies order. Seed 3185, grid 128×96, and 3600 steps are constants. The run prints frame count and writes a metrics JSON. Dependencies are the repo scientific stack (numpy, Pillow, matplotlib); this pass does not pin a per-script lockfile." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
