<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — Morphological realism / specimen match: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The last GIF frame is a sepia two-arm spiral on the same brown ground as the gallery plate. Official CV similarity is 81.9 (12-bin orientation, 24-bin radial FFT, structure-tensor coherency, occupancy) at 800×600 and 16 frames. The plate itself is a stylized pigment field with a 100 µm scale bar, not a micrograph of teeth, so the match is to that plate and not to an SEM. The simulated spiral has more turns than the plate because the domain holds eight critical wavelengths." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md L27–L29: plate is a stylized gallery asset, not an SEM at 2.1 µm <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d/datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md#L27-L29>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm (Drosophila ficusphila)",
        "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm faithfully reproduces Drosophila ficusphila morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila ficusphila specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila ficusphila" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 2.072 µm was measured on D. ficusphila cuticle.",
        "does_not_claim: That the 100 µm sibling slot's alpha/beta power law is this model.",
        "does_not_claim: That the gallery plate is an SEM or a light micrograph of a sex-comb tooth.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Predecessor D. eugracilis is given linear density 2/3 and successor D. grimshawi density 1/2, at geological age 0 Ma, producing λ = 3.108 µm and 4.144 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spiral charge m = 2 is a render choice so the growing mode has the same two-arm layout as the gallery plate.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The assigned detail-tier wavelength λ_c = 2.072 µm (2.072e-6 m, log10 = -5.684) is imposed by choosing D_u at diffusion ratio 20.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979): two-species kinetics with a homogeneous steady state and a limit-cycle regime; the Jacobian used here is the standard linearisation of R_u = a - u + u^2 v, R_v = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Tanaka et al. (2011) and Kopp (2011): sex-comb teeth are a recent, sex-specific bristle innovation under doublesex and Scr.",
        "reported_in_source: Tanaka, Barmina & Kopp (2009): longitudinal sex combs evolve by about 90 degrees of rotation of a transverse row, or by bristles that arise already longitudinal.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952): a reaction-diffusion system can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: No cited sex-comb paper reports a 2.072 µm Turing wavelength, a Schnakenberg parameter table, or a measured tooth-ridge spacing at this tier.",
        "transfer_boundary: The chronoseries order (eugracilis before ficusphila before grimshawi) is the project series of extant species, not a stratigraphic lineage." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila ficusphila (Fig-Breeding Oriental Sophophora Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila ficusphila; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952): a reaction-diffusion system can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg (1979): two-species kinetics with a homogeneous steady state and a limit-cycle regime; the Jacobian used here is the standard linearisation of R_u = a - u + u^2 v, R_v = b - u^2 v. | Tanaka, Barmina & Kopp (2009): longitudinal sex combs evolve by about 90 degrees of rotation of a transverse row, or by bristles that arise already longitudinal. | Tanaka et al. (2011) and Kopp (2011): sex-comb teeth are a recent, sex-specific bristle innovation under doublesex and Scr.; reconstructed_in_script: The assigned detail-tier wavelength λ_c = 2.072 µm (2.072e-6 m, log10 = -5.684) is imposed by choosing D_u at diffusion ratio 20. | Predecessor D. eugracilis is given linear density 2/3 and successor D. grimshawi density 1/2, at geological age 0 Ma, producing λ = 3.108 µm and 4.144 µm. | Spiral charge m = 2 is a render choice so the growing mode has the same two-arm layout as the gallery plate.; transfer_boundary: No cited sex-comb paper reports a 2.072 µm Turing wavelength, a Schnakenberg parameter table, or a measured tooth-ridge spacing at this tier. | The chronoseries order (eugracilis before ficusphila before grimshawi) is the project series of extant species, not a stratigraphic lineage.; does_not_claim: That the gallery plate is an SEM or a light micrograph of a sex-comb tooth. | That 2.072 µm was measured on D. ficusphila cuticle. | That the 100 µm sibling slot's alpha/beta power law is this model.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
